{"name":"Jungle Jam","hex":"#115511","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"jungle","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large, lush, undeveloped, humid forest, especially in a tropical region, thick with vegetation and wildlife; a tropical  rainforest.","Any uncultivated tract of forest or scrub habitat."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["(Of musical beat, rhythm, etc.) resembling the fast-paced drumming of traditional peoples of the jungle."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jungle"},{"term":"jam","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Jamaican Creole."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sweet mixture of fruit boiled with sugar and allowed to congeal. Often spread on bread or toast or used in jam tarts","A difficult situation."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jam"}],"entries":[{"title":"Jungle Jam and Friends: The Radio Show!","blocks":[{"text":"Jungle Jam and Friends: The Radio Show!, or simply Jungle Jam, is a children's radio show with Evangelical Christian themes and humor. The show was created by Jeff Parker and is owned by Fancy Monkey Studios, Inc.. It features voices, writing, and sound editing by Nathan Carlson, Phil Lollar, David Buller, and many others. These people have also been involved in other well-known radio projects, including Adventures in Odyssey."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/ba/JUNGLE_JAM.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jungle_Jam_and_Friends%3A_The_Radio_Show!","wikidata":"Q6312847"},{"title":"Jungle","blocks":[{"text":"A jungle is an area of land covered with dense forest and tangled vegetation, usually in tropical climates. Application of the term has varied greatly during the past century. Because jungles occur on all inhabited landmasses and may incorporate numerous vegetation and land types in different climatic zones, the wildlife of jungles cannot be straightforwardly defined."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/%E1%9E%96%E1%9F%92%E1%9E%9A%E1%9F%83%E1%9E%80%E1%9E%98%E1%9F%92%E1%9E%96%E1%9E%BB%E1%9E%87%E1%9E%B6.jpg/330px-%E1%9E%96%E1%9F%92%E1%9E%9A%E1%9F%83%E1%9E%80%E1%9E%98%E1%9F%92%E1%9E%96%E1%9E%BB%E1%9E%87%E1%9E%B6.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jungle","wikidata":"Q191086"},{"title":"Fruit preserves","blocks":[{"text":"Fruit preserves are preparations of fruits whose main preserving agent is sugar and sometimes acid, often stored in glass jars and used as a condiment or spread."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Fruits_jam_variants.jpg/330px-Fruits_jam_variants.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fruit_preserves","wikidata":"Q74048276"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Tioman_Rainforest.JPG/500px-Tioman_Rainforest.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Tioman_Rainforest.JPG/1280px-Tioman_Rainforest.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Tioman_Rainforest.JPG/500px-Tioman_Rainforest.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Jungle on Tioman Island, Malaysia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATioman_Rainforest.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Puerto_Rico_El_Yunque_1.jpg/500px-Puerto_Rico_El_Yunque_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Puerto_Rico_El_Yunque_1.jpg/1280px-Puerto_Rico_El_Yunque_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign